```trigger
trigger OpportunityTrigger on Opportunity (before insert, before update, before delete, after insert, after update, after delete, after undelete)
{
    fflib_SObjectDomain.triggerHandler(Opportunities.class);
}
```

Notes on the implementation:

- `onValidate()` is fflib's validation hook; `fflib_SObjectDomain.triggerHandler` invokes `validate()` (and therefore `onValidate()`) during the before-insert/before-update phases, so both rules run at the right point in the trigger lifecycle with no extra wiring.
- Each violation is reported via `Error(message, record, field)`, which scopes the error to the `Amount` field of the offending record only and registers it in `fflib_SObjectDomain.Errors`, so other records in the same DML still save and unit tests can assert the errors.
- Rule 2 uses `getOriginal()` (populated on update by fflib from the trigger `Old` map), so it compares against pre-update values: a record already `Closed Won` that changes `Amount` fails, while moving to `Closed Won` with an amount change in the same update passes. On insert the original map is empty, so the check is naturally skipped.
- The loop is bulk-safe (no SOQL, single pass over the records) and null-safe; `compareTo` avoids the `BigDecimal.equals()` scale pitfall when detecting amount changes.

