This is exactly what the scratch org definition file's `objectSettings` block was built for. On the current release it supports two things per object (Account, Case, Contact, Lead, Opportunity):

- **`defaultRecordType: "default"`** – creates the standard ("default") record type on that object, so the vendor package can ship its record types and layout assignments without hitting the "no active record type" error. For Account, the master record type already exists, but explicitly requesting it is harmless and makes the intent clear.
- **`defaultExternalAccess`** – sets the object's organization-wide default at creation time. `Private` gives Opportunity an OWD of Private; `ReadWrite` gives Case an OWD of Public Read/Write (not Read/Write/Transfer, which would be `ReadWriteTransfer`).

